  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.Utility\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A utility class providing static helper methods for the ordering module. It offers three main functionalities: (1) `validateStringField` – validates that a string field is not null or empty, appending a formatted error message to a provided `StringBuilder` and incrementing an error count if validation fails, useful for aggregating multiple field validation errors; (2) `isNullOrEmpty` – a simple null-or-empty check for strings, returning `true` if the string is `null` or has zero length; (3) `getTelemetryClient` – retrieves the Application Insights `TelemetryClient` bean from the Spring `ApplicationContext` via `OrderingConfiguration`, returning `null` if the context is unavailable. This class acts as a shared toolbox across the ordering package, centralizing common validation and telemetry-access logic.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/Utility.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
